            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"Watchfulness, the hastening or fulfillment of God's word, and resurrection or new life.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"Jeremiah 1:11-12\",\"Numbers 17:8\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"Divine election, vindication, and chosen priestly authority.\",\"basis\":[\"Numbers 17:5-10\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"Divine light, fruitfulness, and the illumination of the Holy Spirit via the tabernacle lampstand.\",\"basis\":[\"Exodus 25:33-34\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"Old age, the passing of youth, and white hair (associated with the white/pink blossoms of the tree).\",\"basis\":[\"Ecclesiastes 12:5\"],\"prominence\":\"minority\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"The primary symbolic meaning of watchfulness derives from an explicit Hebrew wordplay in Jeremiah 1:11-12 between 'shaqed' (almond tree) and 'shoqed' (watching). Because the almond is the first tree to blossom in the Middle Eastern spring, it naturally signifies awakening and resurrection, themes further reinforced by the miraculous blooming of Aaron's dead wooden staff.\"}",
